Subject: [PATCH] Recipe extraction lab: reconcile the live-file provenance and
 Phase 3 notes with main bca110e
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

main bca110e (import-overhaul corrections, the Table app session) changed Table's live ingredient-line.ts
(a bare "pepper" is a household seasoning only when measured like one), so the lab's deliberate guard in
tests/parity/provenance.test.ts failed after merging main — the only failure (919 other tests passed).

- src/legacy/PROVENANCE.json: liveTableObserved now records bca110e's file hash as the accepted later
  version; 8e6bd6e's hash is kept in the note. Frozen copies, their hashes, the cb7b56e baseline and
  tests/parity/baseline-snapshot.json are unchanged.
- docs/table/recipe-extraction/PHASE-3-DEPENDENCIES.md: a new §4 records what bca110e changed (per-serving
  rounding toward zero, unit-aware pepper, held pending row edits) and its effect on §2–§3; nothing above it
  was rewritten. The app corrections do not complete or replace the extraction engine.

Lab suite with main merged: 920 passed, 1 expected fail, 11 skipped; package typecheck clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NpRQcZYB2Xf6SyHncApwgZ
